on the disk which is currently logged in.

     Eacè filå entrù iî thió buffeò ió 1¶ byteó long¬ anä iô 
is structured as follows:

          DB   user           ; user number of file
          DB   'FILENAME'     ; name of file
          DB   'TYP'          ; type of file
          DB   ext            ; extent of file*
          DB   0,0            ; uninteresting - leave alone
          DB   rec            ; record count in this extent

ª  exô  ió thå filå extent»  foò DIRLOAD¬  iô ió  thå  firsô 
extenô  numbeò oæ thå file»  foò DIRSLOAD¬  iô ió  thå  lasô 
extent number of the file

:How To Use These Routines

     Thå  DIRÆ  oò DIRFÓ routineó wilì probablù bå  useä  tï 
perforí youò directorù accesó functionó thå vasô majoritù oæ 
thå time®   Giveî á buffer¬  aî ambiguouó filå spec¬  anä  á 
selectioî  flag¬  DIRÆ anä DIRFÓ loaä thå desireä fileó  foò 
yoõ anä theî yoõ caî worë witè thå 16-bytå filå entrieó froí 
there®  Á typicaì callinç sequencå foò DIRÆ oò DIRFÓ is:

          CALL CODEND         ; point to buffer space
          LXI  D,FCB          ; point to FCB of file spec
          MVI  A,1100$0000B   ; select all files in user 0
          CALL DIRF           ; load entries
          JZ   TPAOVFL        ; error condition
          <continue>          ; HL pts to first entry, BC=
                              ;  number of entries
Š
     Iæ  yoõ wisè tï deviatå froí thå "normal¢ uså foò  DIRÆ 
anä DIRFS¬  accesó tï thå routineó useä bù DIRÆ anä DIRFÓ ió 
available®   Á caså iî whicè yoõ maù wanô tï dï thió ió wheî 
yoõ  arå interesteä iî fileó whicè matcè morå thaî onå  filå 
spec¬  sucè aó *.ASÍ anä *.TXT®   Á typicaì callinç sequencå 
for this type of access is:

;  Setup
